# The Dockerfile COPYs exactly the paths it needs explicitly (config.yaml,
# src/pricepoint, api, models, data/03_marts,
# data/02_processed/feature_engineered_data.parquet) -- this file exists
# as a second line of defense against an accidental `COPY . .` pulling in
# the 791MB raw dataset, .git history, or node_modules.
.git/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Everything under data/ except what the Dockerfile copies explicitly:
# data/03_marts/ (Warehouse/history endpoint) and
# feature_engineered_data.parquet (predict endpoint's DuckDB
# predicate-pushdown source) -- the other two files in 02_processed/
# (canonical_products_e5.parquet, anomalies_flagged.parquet, ~280MB
# combined) are never read by a live API request.
data/00_raw/
data/01_interim/
data/02_processed/
!data/02_processed/feature_engineered_data.parquet
data/03_external/
data/_run_reports/

frontend/
node_modules/
dashboard/
notebooks/
tests/
docs/
plots/
scripts/
.github/

*.md
!README.md
